Changed file: Sources/BeamfallManager/ManagerApp.swift

Intent:
feat(apps): cards load artwork from server-declared paths, entity cards included

TVArtworkFrame, the TV card labels, and the Manager's PosterImage now
take the item's declared artwork path instead of constructing media
poster URLs by Media-ID convention. A nil path renders the existing
fallback frame without issuing a request (the contract: absent means
no artwork exists). Entity cards gain artwork for free — the declared
path points at /api/entity/artwork/... where they previously probed a
media path that always 404ed. Buckets unchanged (w640 tvOS, w320
Manager); the in-memory poster cache is now keyed by artwork path.
No by-convention fallback retained: the TV Snapshot persists only
libraries/navigation/layouts (never SourceItems) and the Manager keeps
no item cache, so no at-rest item shape predates the field.

