Changed file: Sources/BeamfallMobile/MobileRootView.swift

Intent:
AUDIT-APPLE-4 start StoreKit Transaction.updates listener at app launch

The paywall previously owned PremiumStore as a per-present @StateObject and
started the Transaction.updates listener on onAppear, so Ask-to-Buy and
background-renewal completions were missed while the paywall was closed
(App Review OS8-1).

Own PremiumStore at the app root (BeamfallMobileApp @StateObject), start
startTransactionListener() at launch via a root-scene .task, and inject the
store into MobileRootView -> MobilePremiumView. startTransactionListener() is
idempotent (guards updateTask == nil), so the single launch call plus the
paywall's still-idempotent start() cannot double-start or leak the listener.

Verify: PremiumTransactionListenerLaunchTests (make gate-host, host-runnable,
no iOS binary) structurally asserts the app root starts the listener at launch
and the paywall no longer creates its own store, plus a behavioral idempotency
check on the launch-time API.

